[122.089747, "o", "\"\"\"Build the churn feature table: python -m churn.build_features --data <dir> --out <file.parquet>\\n\\nThis implementation mirrors the live scoring service by ensuring that, for each prediction\\npoint, only rows that were *visible* in the warehouse at that moment are used. Visibility is\\ndetermined by the `_loaded_at` column present in every extract CSV (except `scoring_points`).\\n\\nThe original implementation relied on the full tables, which could leak future rows that were\\nback‑filled after a prediction timestamp. The revised `build` function iterates over each row\\nin `scoring_points` and filters each source table by both the event timestamp **and** the\\n`_loaded_at` timestamp before computing features. The logic for each feature is equivalent to\\nthe original helpers (`activity_features`, `tenure_days`, `latest_status`, etc.) but applied\\nto the point‑in‑time subset.\\n\"\"\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[122.089809, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n"]
